  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "No network code (checked in source)",
      "items": [
        "None of the app's sources use network APIs; the only https:// is a brew.sh link the user can click (ApplicationsView.swift:343)",
        "Checked in source, not enforced by macOS: the app is not sandboxed (MyMacCleaner.entitlements:5-6)",
        "App-wide check bans URLSession, URLRequest and Sparkle (verify-safety-contract.sh:960); network APIs and https:// are banned in SafetyContract and named files (:952, :973) and in CleanerCore (verify-cleanercore-contract.sh:122)",
        "No update channel: UpdateCapability has one case, .unavailable (UpdateCapability.swift:3-8)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Logs carry counts, not evidence",
      "items": [
        "Scan diagnostics go to AdaptiveSilentDiagnostics, which drops them (AdaptiveScanSession.swift:165-167)",
        "SafetyDiagnosticLogger writes to the macOS unified log and takes only an event code plus per-class counts (SafetyDiagnosticLogger.swift:4-21, RedactingDiagnostic.swift:43-56)",
        "Callers: StartupItemsService failures, the open-file check when its listing fails, and receipt-history events in AdaptiveTrustSession"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "One change to user files, narrowly gated",
      "items": [
        "Only ~/Library/Caches/com.apple.iconservices.store files idle 15+ minutes and not held open can become candidates; if the open-file listing fails, none can",
        "A move needs the digest (hash) of the plan on screen; the plan's roots are rescanned and checked again first",
        "FoundationTrashAdapter re-checks identity, then calls trashItem",
        "Receipts (Application Support, owner-only 0700, out of backups) hold item paths hex-encoded and Trash locations; only a redacted summary leaves the store (PolicyEvaluation.swift:178-183, AppSupportReceiptStore.swift:463-476, 532-550)",
        "The app also writes and prunes its own receipts (ReceiptHistoryCoordinator.swift:141-147)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Scope notes",
      "items": [
        "Not shown: Duplicates (hashes file contents), Space Lens, Startup Items, Ports, System Health",
        "Six roots: ~/Library/Caches, ~/Library/Logs, the per-user temp folder ($TMPDIR), Downloads, Desktop, Documents",
        "Open-file check reads the whole lsof listing of files the user's processes hold open, then keeps only paths under the roots, in memory",
        "Model stores parsed: Hugging Face (HF) hub, Ollama models, and a user-picked directory; model weights are never read",
        "A picked directory goes straight to the Adaptive view model, not through the trust session (AdaptiveExperienceViewModel.swift:245-262); for HF_HOME and OLLAMA_MODELS the app only checks whether they are set",
        "LM Studio and MLX are never scanned as stores; they appear only as app presence, workload labels or association evidence",
        "Legacy projection turns findings into the older ScanResult rows that Home and Disk Cleaner show, without policy verdicts; Home can reveal a listed file in Finder",
        "Sources as of main, November 2026"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
